-a50a-babd4de5fa31","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"ed07-b103-3e7b-4c50"},{"link_uuid":"386926c3-1b35-488a-852f-71cf88e751ad","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"b8f7-65be-ec00-4844"}],"description":"## Observation\n\n`tests/scripts/bridge/test_bridge_fsck_keyset_prev.py::test_store_snapshot_survives_git_maintenance_but_still_catches_mutation` failed once in a full `make verify` (2026-11-11 00:20-00:50 PST, worktree fixver-epic at commit 4d21c744977, which does not touch bridge fsck). Line 254 `lock.unlink()` raised `FileNotFoundError` for `<tmp>/churn/.tickets-tracker/.git/objects/maintenance.lock`: the test wrote the file, `_store_snapshot` ran, and the file was gone before the test removed it. The same test passed 6 of 6 times run alone right afterwards. The earlier bug `chewed-illicit-blacklemur` (closed) described a race between this test and git auto-maintenance on macOS.\n\n## Hypotheses (unproven)\n\n- A git process started inside the test fixture (auto-maintenance or gc) runs in the background and removes `objects/maintenance.lock` when it finishes.\n- The earlier fix narrowed the race but did not remove it; host load under `make verify` (4 xdist workers) widens it.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A deterministic reproduction (for example, holding the background git process or forcing auto-maintenance in the fixture) shows the cause.\n- [ ] The test no longer depends on timing: the fixture disables git auto-maintenance/gc for its repos, or the test uses a lock path no git process deletes.\n- [ ] The test passes 200 consecutive runs under `pytest -n 4` load.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["relates_to","b8f7-65be-ec00-4844"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"